@startuml
title RuleSphere - Activity Diagram\n06. REST / gRPC Evaluation | UC-21..24
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #E9F8ED
skinparam activityBorderColor #496477
|Consumer Application|
start
:Send input, credential, routing context\nand optional version pin;
|Runtime Admission|
:Validate credential and Tenant/Workspace access;
if (Authorized?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Return authentication / access error;
  stop
endif
if (Exact version pin supplied?) then (yes)
  :Find exact eligible version in local artifact store;
  if (Pinned version available and eligible?) then (yes)
  else (no)
    :Return REST 412 or documented gRPC\nprecondition error; no fallback to Active;
    stop
  endif
else (no)
  :Resolve configured sticky Canary / cohort selection\nor latest eligible node-local Active;
  if (Selected snapshot available?) then (yes)
  else (no)
    :Return protocol-defined availability error;
    stop
  endif
endif
:Bind graph, schemas, dependencies and libraries\nas one atomic snapshot;
:Validate input against bound schema;
if (Input contract valid?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Return client contract error before evaluation;
  stop
endif
|Graph Executor|
:Create execution context and trace; set healthy;
while (More nodes and execution healthy?) is (yes)
  :Select next node in topological order;
  if (Branch activated?) then (yes)
    :Evaluate node in fixed execution context;
    if (Node succeeded?) then (yes)
      :Record result, matched node and activated branches;
    else (no)
      if (Qualifying error and valid typed fallback configured?) then (yes)
        :Use fallback and record fallback use;
      else (no)
        :Record attributable error and mark failed;
      endif
    endif
  else (no)
    :Skip inactive branch;
  endif
endwhile (no)
:Finalize execution outcome and trace tree;
|Runtime Response|
:Dispatch safe asynchronous evidence capture\n(details in diagram 07);
if (Execution succeeded?) then (yes)
  :Return result, executionId\nand authorized version metadata;
else (no)
  :Return attributable protocol-defined execution error;
endif
|Consumer Application|
:Receive response;
stop
legend bottom
  Normal evaluation has no synchronous Control Plane dependency.
  Mid-request publication never replaces the bound atomic snapshot.
  Trace persistence does not block this flow; failures follow observable operational policy.
endlegend
@enduml
